<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Mažuranić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1814–1890</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Mažuranić was a Croatian poet, lawyer and politician who served as ban of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> from 1873 to 1880, the first ban not of noble birth. His epic poem The Death of Smail-aga Čengić (1846) is a classic of Croatian literature. As ban he modernised the administration, separated the courts from the government and reformed the schools.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-mazuranic.jpg" alt="Ivan Mažuranić" width="234" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ivan_Mazuranic_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
